# These artifacts are content-addressed evidence, not ordinary text. Their
# loaders require canonical JSON terminated by exactly one LF, and several
# verify the file's SHA-256 against a registered or reviewed blob. Any
# end-of-line translation on checkout changes those bytes, so on a Windows
# host with core.autocrlf=true the committed zero-access declarations and
# production registries become unreadable and the authority check they exist
# to perform is never reached.
#
# -text disables all conversion in both directions, so the working tree always
# holds exactly the committed bytes.
*.json -text
